cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KazStem in research, please cite this software."
title: "KazStem: an ambiguity-preserving Kazakh morphological analyzer and generator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nuriyev
    given-names: Amir
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-08-10
repository-code: "https://github.com/amir-nuriyev/KazStem"
url: "https://github.com/amir-nuriyev/KazStem"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - Kazakh
  - morphology
  - morphological analysis
  - lemmatization
  - finite-state transducers
  - natural language processing
abstract: >-
  KazStem is an ambiguity-preserving morphological analyzer and generator for
  Kazakh. It combines finite-state morphology, bounded productive analysis,
  optional Constraint Grammar disambiguation, and candidate-constrained neural
  ranking behind a MyStem-like command-line interface and a typed Python API.
